# BEGIN check_cycle
# The check after pickup in the cycle (PickPlaceOptions::check_after_pickup),
# one action at a time: the check pose clear of the planning margin at every
# depth and slot, and what the via costs; the two-leg carry and its dwell;
# the picture and the finder; the measured grip against the truth; the
# corrected lower and set down; the refusals (refused, slipped, retaken); the
# plausibility test on the measured grip (a check camera turned across its
# view fails as a camera fault; turned about its axis, unseen); a yaw grip
# placed square in slot 1; a leg 2 with no path (kNoPath); whole camera
# cycles with the pallet camera's calibration off, with and without the
# check, and with the check camera's off too; stage 6's fixes (a blocked
# set-down's record, records across a Reset, pausing on a skipped step); and
# stage 7's (a Reset noticed anywhere fails the cycle, no pick with a module
# on the tool, the measured grip its module's only).
#   bazel test --config=opt //:check_cycle_test --test_output=all
# One source, two targets, so that the two halves run side by side: the whole
# camera cycles (the CheckCycles suite, whose shared setup runs nine cycles
# and is about two thirds of the time) in check_cycle_batch_test, and
# everything else in check_cycle_test. A new suite lands in check_cycle_test.
# Sharding instead would repeat that setup in every shard.
[cc_test(
    name = name,
    size = "medium",
    args = ["--gtest_filter=" + gtest_filter],
    srcs = ["tests/check_cycle_test.cc"],
    data = CELL_FILES,
